    <string name="onb_welcome_title">Welcome to Aira</string>
    <string name="onb_welcome_body">Aira is a diary of the weather you actually experience: where you were, whether you were outside, and what the weather did to you.</string>
    <string name="onb_why_title">Why Aira needs your location</string>
    <string name="onb_why_body">Weather changes from place to place. Aira uses your approximate location to fetch the weather where you are. Your data stays on your phone. The only thing sent out is a weather request with a rounded location.</string>
    <string name="onb_location_title">Approximate location</string>
    <string name="onb_location_body">Allow location access so Aira can find the weather where you are.</string>
    <string name="onb_background_title">Location in the background</string>
    <string name="onb_background_body">To keep your diary while the app is closed, Aira needs location access all the time. On the next screen choose \"Allow all the time\". Without it Aira only records while you have it open.</string>
    <string name="onb_activity_title">Steps and activity</string>
    <string name="onb_activity_body">Aira counts your steps to tell whether you were walking or sitting still.</string>
    <string name="onb_notifications_title">Notifications</string>
    <string name="onb_notifications_body">Allow notifications so Aira can warn you about rain, heat and strong sun.</string>
    <string name="onb_battery_title">Keep logging reliable</string>
    <string name="onb_battery_body">Some phones stop background apps to save battery. Open the battery settings and set Aira to \"Unrestricted\" or turn off battery optimisation so your diary has no gaps. This is optional.</string>
    <string name="onb_finish_title">You are all set</string>
    <string name="onb_finish_body">Aira will now check every 5 minutes whether you are indoors or outdoors and walking, still or travelling. Recording pauses at night, from 23:00 to 06:00. You can change this later in Settings.</string>

